; 15-repl-stdin: at the REPL the program's input is the console's: read-line, read-byte, read-bytes, read-buffer and read-all take the input that comes after the line being run (a line's rest after the bytes taken is input again), in a def, in a function, in a map; then read-all takes the rest, and the session ends
(def {l} (read-line))
this line is data for read-line, not code (or a call)
(print (repr l) (len l))
(def {c} (read-byte))
Z
(print c (code-char c))
(fun {ask q} {do (write q "? ") (read-line)})
(ask "name")
answer to ask
(list (ask "first") (ask "second"))
one
two
(map (fn {x} {list x (read-line)}) {1 2 3})
m1

m3 with spaces   
(read-bytes stdin 5)
12345(+ 1 2)
(def {b} (buffer 4))
(read-buffer stdin b)
WXYZ
(print b (from-bytes b))
(list (read-byte) (read-byte) (read-byte))
xy
(+ 2 2)
(dotimes {i 2} (print i (read-line)))
line for 0
line for 1
(output-of (print (read-line)))
captured
(try (read-line) &err)
tried
(repr (read-all))
all the rest
(+ 1 2) is not run: it is data now
"and so is this"
